{"scenario":"cas-connection-lost-rejects-cpdus","rows":["B-0276","B-0277","B-0324","B-0403","A-0235","C-0739","C-0866","C-0911","C-1120","C-1250","C-1251","K-0067","K-0074"],"source":"Ed4 B.7.2.8, p.B-35; C.7.5.2.1, p.C-112; C.7.5.6, p.C-117","description":"A peer that never answers our ARQ data is given up once it has been silent for sixteen acknowledgement waits: at the end of a retransmission the DTS declares the connection lost and rejects the C_PDU, and the CAS breaks the link locally.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":25,"block_ms":4800}]},"cas":{"max_links":4,"link_request_timeout_ms":60000,"link_request_retries":2,"first_data_timeout_ms":120000},"dts":{"ack_wait_ms":60000}},"note":"Conn 1 binds SAP 5 for ARQ at 0. Link setup as cas/make-called-accept: the peer's PHYSICAL LINK REQUEST (Ed4) at 2000, our PHYSICAL LINK ACCEPTED out at 52000, and the link made when that transmission ends at 57550 (B-0213, B-0400): link_state linked and cas.first_data/0.0.1.3 (B-0215). The peer is recorded Ed4 (B-0408) and the 16-bit family is in force. At 61000 the peer's first DATA C_PDU arrives: a DATA-ONLY (FSN 0, C_PDU START and END, both window flags, EOT 10) with 'ping' for SAP 9, which no client has bound, so the SIS discards it (A-0235); it is the first DATA C_PDU by ARQ, so cas.first_data stops (B-0215, B-0403), and it owes an acknowledgement. At 61500 conn 1 sends an ARQ U_PDU 'pong' to SAP 9 at 0.0.1.3 (TTL 0); the soft link exists (A-0194), so it goes down as an ARQ C_PDU (10 bytes: the S_PDU with TTD and 'pong') and dts.ttd runs to its TTD. At 78000 it goes in a DATA-ACK (FSN 0, RX LWE 1, DELIVER IN ORDER as the SIS asked, both window flags, C-1128), 32 bytes, 2 blocks, EOT 20, with an ACK-ONLY copy in the fill (C-1154); dts.ack_wait/0.0.1.3 starts at 88350 (C-1120). Retransmissions are DATA-ONLY (29 bytes, 2 blocks, EOT 20) with a PADDING D_PDU (11 bytes, EOT 10) in the spare bytes (C-1154). From now on the peer is silent. At each dts.ack_wait expiry FSN 0 is taken to have failed and is retransmitted (C-0911, C-1120): LBT 3000 after our own transmission (K-0074), then contention, then the 2-block transmission (10350 ms), then dts.ack_wait again; the peer's silence is timed from 88350, the end of the first transmission after its last answer (the DATA-ONLY at 61000) that left us awaiting one, and the DTS checks at each expiry, and at the end of each of our transmissions to the peer, whether it has lasted 16 answer waits, 960000 ms (C-1250). The tenth expiry at 1045500 is 957150 ms on, short of it, so FSN 0 goes again; the end of that transmission at 1076850 is 988500 ms on, so no dts.ack_wait starts: the DTS sends D_CONNECTION_LOST to the CAS and ends the connection itself (C-0739, C-1251): the unconfirmed C_PDU is rejected with a local reason (C-0866), so dts.ttd, with nothing left, is cancelled. The CAS breaks the link locally, with no C_PDU to the peer (B-0277, B-0324): link_state unlinked and C_PHYSICAL_LINK_BROKEN to the SIS. Fixture: preamble 600, flush 150, 25 bytes and 4800 ms a block, so an n-block transmission lasts 750 + 4800 n ms, and the EOT of a D_PDU starting in block b of n is ceil((4800 (n - b) + 150) / 500): 10, 20, 30 for 1, 2, 3 blocks to go (C-0104, C-1043). Addresses 0.0.1.2 (this node) and 0.0.1.3 take address size 3 (C-0133). A CAS-1 C_PDU of one octet in a type 8 D_PDU fills a block exactly (25 bytes; EOT and reception window 10), C_PDU IDs from 0 in each node's own sequence (C-1040), EOW 0. Seed 0 draws uniform(16) = 15, 4, 15, 12, 11, 10, 1, 12, 3, 6, 9, 6, 11, 15, 9, 11, 5, 6: contention waits 45000, 12000, 45000, 36000, 33000, 30000, 3000, 36000, 9000, 18000, 27000, 18000, 33000, 45000, 27000, 33000, 15000, 18000 ms (K-0080)."}
